 trials do we need?</article-title><source>J Clin Epi</source><year>2009</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>461</fpage><lpage>463</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jclinepi.2009.01.011</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zwarenstein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Treweek</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What kind of randomized trials do we need?</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><year>2009</year><volume>180</volume><fpage>998</fpage><lpage>1000</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19372438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zwarenstein</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Treweek</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What kind of randomized trials do patients and clinicians need?</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2009</year><volume>150</volume><comment>JC5-2, JC5-3.</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19451559</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vallv&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A critical review of the pragmatic clinical trial [in Spanish]</article-title><source>Med Clin (Barc)</source><year>2003</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>384</fpage><lpage>388</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1157/13052554</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>US Food and Drug Administration, Guidance for Institutional Review Boards and Clinical Investigators 1998 Update</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.fda.gov/ScienceResearch/SpecialTopics/RunningClinicalTrials/GuidancesInformationSheetsandNotices/ucm117847.htm"/></citation></ref><